title: AWS STS Role Chaining Anomaly
id: 00752337-961d-47da-b710-10c02464d0e9
status: experimental
description: Detects AssumeRole chains where an assumed-role session immediately assumes another role repeatedly, a role-chaining pattern used to pivot across permissions and obscure the originating identity.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1078/004/
logsource:
  product: aws
  service: cloudtrail
detection:
  selection:
    eventName: 'AssumeRole'
    userIdentity.type: 'AssumedRole'
  timeframe: 10m
  condition: selection | count() by userIdentity.arn > 5
  condition: selection
fields:
  - userIdentity.arn
  - eventName
  - sourceIPAddress
falsepositives:
  - Automation that legitimately chains roles
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.lateral_movement
  - attack.t1078.004
